\ The Fibonacci repro from the parameter-inference bug, built as locked
\ interpreter-free AOT with no type annotation anywhere in the file.
\
\ Under the lock any interpreter fallback of any category rejects the build, so a
\ successful build is itself the proof that the `+` inside `[ swap over + ] dip`
\ compiles concretely. It only does so because the freeze-time pass proves
\ `fib-step`'s three parameters and the dip-invoked quotation's from the call
\ sites, then codegen unboxes them at entry.
\
\ Printing is omitted. A `.` would reach the generic `inspect`, whose dispatch
\ site keeps two cold interpreter-callback branches the lock rejects, so the
\ repro cannot print the number it computes until that gap closes. Correctness is
\ observed through the exit status instead: a wrong answer divides by zero, and a
\ clean exit is the pass. The computed values are checked separately by
\ `param_type_inference.1z`, which builds without the lock and can print.

fib-step: ( a b n -- result ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop drop ] [
    1 - [ swap over + ] dip fib-step
  ] if
] ;

fib: ( n -- n ) [
  dup 2 < [ ] [
    0 1 <rot- fib-step
  ] if
] ;

30 fib 832040 = [ ] [ 1 0 / drop ] if
